---
import Slide from "../../components/Slide.astro"
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'

import notebook from "../../img/python/notebook.png"
import ext_python from "../../img/python/vsc-ext-python.jpg"
import ext_jupyter from "../../img/python/vsc-ext-jupyter.jpg"
import jupyter_new_file from "../../img/python/jupyter-new-file.jpg"
---
<Slide t1="Python Quick-Start">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">We are using Python configured for Jupyter Notebooks</li>
        <li class="fragment">Notebook environment: mix of code and documentation</li>
        <li class="fragment">Notebooks (<code>.ipynb</code>) can be
            run inside Visual Studio Code</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Visual Studio Code Extensions">
    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image src={ext_python} alt="" width="600" />
    </div>
    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image src={ext_jupyter} alt="" width="600" />
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Setup: Jupyter Notebooks">
    <ul class="text-sm-2">
        <li>Need to open a folder (or workspace)</li>
        <li>Then: create and save <em>Jupyter Notebook</em> (<code>.ipynb</code>)</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image src={jupyter_new_file} alt="" width="600" />
    </div>

    <ol class="text-sm-2">
        <li><code>Select Another Kernel...</code></li>
        <li><code>Python Environments...</code></li>
        <li><code>Create Python Environment</code></li>
        <li><code>Venv</code></li>
    </ol>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Notebook inside VS Code">
    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ notebook }
            alt="VS Code Python Notebook"
            height="400"
            width="600" />
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Notebook Structure">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Cells can be <em>executable code</em>
            or <em>Markdown text</em></li>
        <li class="fragment">Library management (one shot) via <code>%pip</code></li>
        <li class="fragment">Incremental, exploratory development</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>
